<title>USA: BTG Q4 shr loss $0.05 vs profit $0.11.</title>
<headline>BTG Q4 shr loss $0.05 vs profit $0.11.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				   Qtr	  Qtr	Year	Year</p>
<p>				 Ended	Ended     Ended     Ended</p>
<p>			     3/31/97    3/31/96   3/31/97   3/31/97</p>
<p> Total revenue	   $90,010    $59,752  $400,033  $213,558</p>
<p> Operating income	    328	1,563    12,042     7,489</p>
<p> Net (loss) income	  (481)	 700     4,271     2,954</p>
<p>Earnings (loss)</p>
<p>  per share		 (0.05)	0.11	0.60	0.47</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>common/equivalent</p>
<p>  shares outstanding     8,811	6,297     7,141     6,233</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said fourth quarter results were affected by unanticipated events including cost pressures associated with the rapid expansion, increased costs of investment in current projects, and one-time charges, including higher than exptected costs of consolidating Washington-area facilities, a client's bankruptcy and an increase in reserves associated with other commercial business.</p>
<p>Full company name is BTG Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
